  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 204 PM EST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\n- Mild and dry through mid week\n\nSystems are moving across the Great Lakes quickly. A short wave\nover southern Ontario nosing into eastern Lower is presently\nmoving east and clouds are rapidly dissipating as ridging moves\nin. This short wave ridge will move overhead tonight and Monday\nmorning before warm air advection clouds associated with the next\nshort wave trek east from Wisconsin Monday afternoon. The\natmosphere is dry and we won't see any precipitation from those\nclouds. \n\nThe weak ridging (h8 temps near +8c) for the next few days will \nkeep high temperatures above normal through Wednesday with highs \nin the 55-60 degree range.\n\n- Showers mid week, then cooler\n\nThe next chance of rain is Wednesday afternoon (30%-40%).\nAn eastern Pacific short wave will move across the Rockies and\ncarve out a mid Mississippi Valley trough. That, in turn, will\npull short wave energy south from southern Canada resulting in a\nhigher amplitude trough over the eastern half of the country.\nWe may see some light rain from the various short waves moving\nthrough the flow. Highest pops will be near the lake shore were a\nnorth/south band of lake enhanced rain will develop...aided by the\ncolder air drawn south into the upper trough.  \n\nH8 temperatures will fall to -8c by Friday morning as colder air\nflows south in the trough. That'll result in highs in the mid 40s\nagain.\n\nGenerally dry conditions are expected beginning Thursday and\ncarrying through next weekend as the effects of the upper trough\nmove east.",
